Learning lvl 1 books is useful.
Learning lvl 2 books is likely useful depending on your Intelligence
and XL.
Lvl 3 is a bit of a toss up.  I'd hate to turn a spellbook of identify
or spellbook of remove curse to dust, but on the other hand, those
could be quite useful spells in the early game, too.  When I start
reading these depends on my intelligence.  If I'm >=3D 85% success rate,
I'll read one.
High level books simply aren't worthwhile, since you might lose the
spellbook, and even if you learn the spell, you can't cast it.

speaking of intelligence stats, I think not alchemizing potions is one
of the things I find oddest about many nethack players.  I understand
not polypiling:  it can be tedious, and it's confusing at first what
to do.  but I just don't understand why people would quaff potions of
healing when after a few dips, they could instead have a stack of
blessed full healing.  or blessed gain ability.  It seems odd to me to
see dumplogs of folks ascending with only 14 Int or only 120 HP.  The
question is not whether you should alchemize or not.  The question is
when you want to quaff the blessed full healing and when you want to
quaff blessed gain ability.

As to the question of when to start, the answer is as soon as you have
enough speed and gain energy to get what you need.  If you can raise
your hitpoints from 60 to 76 by using 5 potions, isn't that helpful?
not as helpful as using 7 potions to go from 60 to 92, but still
helpful.

To me, the potion of gain energy would be better named a potion of
alchemy, since I'll rarely use one for anything other than alchemy.


